WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.876
What does a program do while it runs?

2
00:00:03.256 --> 00:00:03.982
Let's watch.

3
00:00:04.932 --> 00:00:06.492
This program counts the

4
00:00:06.492 --> 00:00:08.064
marks of fifty or more.

5
00:00:08.444 --> 00:00:09.896
passed starts at zero.

6
00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.962
For forty-five, the test

7
00:00:11.962 --> 00:00:13.756
fails, so nothing changes.

8
00:00:14.136 --> 00:00:16.104
For eighty, the test passes

9
00:00:16.104 --> 00:00:17.610
and passed becomes one.

10
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.348
Sixty-two passes too, so passed is

11
00:00:20.348 --> 00:00:22.598
two, and the program prints two.

12
00:00:23.548 --> 00:00:26.236
Here is the same program as a flowchart.

13
00:00:26.616 --> 00:00:28.752
Take the next mark and test it.

14
00:00:29.132 --> 00:00:30.992
Forty-five fails, so we go

15
00:00:30.992 --> 00:00:32.510
back for the next one.

16
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.978
Eighty passes, so we add one.

17
00:00:35.358 --> 00:00:36.636
Sixty-two passes too.

18
00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:39.104
With no marks left, we print

19
00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:40.394
the count and stop.

20
00:00:41.344 --> 00:00:43.012
Python reads the function

21
00:00:43.012 --> 00:00:44.698
first, but runs nothing.

22
00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.766
Line five calls greet with the name Ada.

23
00:00:48.146 --> 00:00:50.624
Inside, text joins Hi and the name.

24
00:00:51.004 --> 00:00:53.200
Return hands it back, msg gets

25
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.898
it, and print shows it.

26
00:00:55.848 --> 00:00:58.014
Selection sort finds the smallest

27
00:00:58.014 --> 00:01:00.102
bar, with j scanning and min

28
00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:01.944
remembering the best so far.

29
00:01:02.324 --> 00:01:05.378
Then it swaps that bar to the front, at i.

30
00:01:05.758 --> 00:01:08.218
Round by round the sorted part grows,

31
00:01:08.398 --> 00:01:10.642
and the counters add up the work.

32
00:01:11.592 --> 00:01:12.990
Binary search for 37.

33
00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:15.176
The middle holds 22, too

34
00:01:15.176 --> 00:01:17.156
small, so lo jumps past it.

35
00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:19.162
The new middle holds 37.

36
00:01:19.542 --> 00:01:21.576
Found it, in just two looks.

37
00:01:22.526 --> 00:01:25.058
Recursion: fib of four calls fib of

38
00:01:25.058 --> 00:01:27.938
three and fib of two, and each of those

39
00:01:27.938 --> 00:01:30.362
calls again, down to one and zero.

40
00:01:30.742 --> 00:01:32.476
The answers climb back up,

41
00:01:32.656 --> 00:01:33.892
adding as they go.

42
00:01:34.272 --> 00:01:37.002
The yellow calls repeat work already done.

43
00:01:37.952 --> 00:01:39.860
This loop should add up the

44
00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.720
marks, but it prints nine.

45
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.034
The bug: total is set to zero inside the

46
00:01:45.034 --> 00:01:47.566
loop, so it starts again every time.

47
00:01:47.946 --> 00:01:50.580
The fix moves that line above the loop.

48
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.520
Now it prints twenty-one.

49
00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.428
Trace it, draw it, watch it run: that

50
00:01:56.428 --> 00:01:58.672
is how code starts to make sense.
